WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:05.040
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.343 --> 00:00:08.524
Give me one minute and I'll show you
how Cloud Pub/Sub can help you

00:00:08.524 --> 00:00:11.364
keep your services
reliably communicating with each other.

00:00:11.694 --> 00:00:14.321
Cloud Pub/Sub is an asynchronous
messaging service,

00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:18.330
which means it helps your tools send,
receive, and filter events or data steams.

00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:22.697
It gives you durable message storage,
scalable in-order message delivery,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.886
consistently high availability
and performance at any scale.

00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:29.434
And Pub/Sub runs in any Google Cloud
region in the world

00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:32.559
so you can easily use it in Jakarta,
Frankfort, or Montreal.

00:00:32.679 --> 00:00:34.228
And of course, everywhere else.

00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:36.691
You also don't have to provision Pub/Sub.

00:00:36.691 --> 00:00:39.382
It scales global data delivery
auto-magically.

00:00:39.382 --> 00:00:41.490
From zero to millions
of messages per second.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.432
With Pub/Sub, data producers
don't need to change anything

00:00:45.432 --> 00:00:47.437
when the consumers of their data change.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.897
Just publish once
and let us manage distribution.

00:00:50.465 --> 00:00:53.066
This let's more of your services
be entirely stateless.

00:00:53.882 --> 00:00:57.263
You set up Pub/Sub between services
or applications by defining topics

00:00:57.263 --> 00:00:59.322
and then subscriptions,
which allow services

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:01.768
to receive the messages
published on those topics.

00:01:03.286 --> 00:01:05.901
This means one-to-many communications
gets much simpler.

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:09.278
So you can spread batch image analysis
over multiple workers

00:01:09.278 --> 00:01:12.283
or send logs from your security system
to archiving, processing,

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:13.554
and analytic services.

00:01:14.013 --> 00:01:16.810
Or, if you got a steady stream of data,
you can use Pub/Sub

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:20.233
to steam that data into BigQuery
or Dataflow for intelligent processing.

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:23.563
Pub/Sub is really handy for notification
when something bad happens,

00:01:23.563 --> 00:01:26.614
so you can page the right teams
if a system or service goes down.

00:01:27.451 --> 00:01:30.224
So, next time you need a way
to connect multiple services,

00:01:30.224 --> 00:01:33.843
applications, or data sources,
take a minute to try out Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:01:34.616 --> 00:01:37.477
Learn more at <i>cloud.google.com/pubsub</i>

00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:42.117
♪ [music] ♪

